# Ōzakura pilot v2 — Prologue + Chapter 1 (source script)
# Compiled by production/pipeline/vn/compile_script.py into v2/script.json and the voice job list.
#
# Syntax
#   == scene_id | Dev-chart title
#   > narration
#   who: "English" || 日本語            spoken line (日本語 is what gets voiced; "-" = unvoiced)
#   who<expr>: ...                      change that character's sprite expression first (outfit kept)
#   kohei(face): ...                    Kōhei's face-window expression
#   who(expr): ...                      any speaker shown only in a face window (e.g. an interlude's POV character)
#   @show who outfit_expr pos  @hide who  @hideall  @move who pos
#   @bg name [cut|fade|slow]  @cg name [cut|fade|slow]  @cg -
#   @bgm name  @bgm -   @sfx name   @wait seconds   @flash white
#   @card text   @chapter n | title   @mode interlude Label   @mode normal   @endchapter n
#   @hold on / @hold off   taps don't skip the waits and crossfades in between (the wordless cold open)
#   {term|gloss}  Japanese term shown with a small English gloss (style guide §5); if notes.txt has the term,
#                 it's also underlined and opens a translator's note when tapped
#
# Names in the Japanese lines are in kana until their kanji are chosen (pilot-notes fix 14).

== cold_open | Cold open
# P.0 (outline, Oct 18): a flash-forward to the misty walk into the distortion. No voices, no narration.
@hold on
@bg black cut
@bgm -
@wait 1.2
@cg cg_cold_mirror slow
@wait 2.6
@cg cg_cold_hand
@wait 2.6
@cg cg_cold_mist
@wait 3.4
@cg cg_cold_mirror
@wait 2.6
@cg - cut
@bg black cut
@wait 1.4
@hold off
@chapter 1 | The House Next Door

== c1_morning | Mornings at the Fujisawas
@card Monday, April 7
@bg bg_kohei_room_day
@bgm daily
> My alarm goes off at 5:40.  #c1_0001
> I'm usually awake before it. I lie there for the full ten seconds anyway, as a matter of principle, listening to the house.  #c1_0002
> The water heater ticking. A crow on the power line. Nothing from downstairs.  #c1_0003
> Second year of high school starts today. It doesn't feel like anything starts. It feels like Monday.  #c1_0004
> I get up.  #c1_0005
@bg bg_fujisawa_kitchen
> The rice was on the timer last night, so the kitchen already smells like steam. Eggs, the leftover spinach, the last of the frozen {karaage|fried chicken}. Two lunch boxes, side by side on the counter.  #c1_0006
> I've gotten fast at this. Fast enough to do it while reading the whiteboard on the fridge.  #c1_0007
> Kendo: Monday, Wednesday, Friday and Saturday morning. Hoshino Kitchen: Tuesday, Thursday and Sunday. A red circle around the 18, Akane's clinic day. All of it in my handwriting.  #c1_0008
> All of it except the bottom line, which still says "Garbage: burnables, Mon/Thu" in Dad's. He wrote it last spring. I've never written over it.  #c1_0009
> The {fusuma|sliding door} to Mom's room is closed. It usually is.  #c1_0010
@wait 0.6
@show akane school_sleepy c
