> This week it's the best walk in Shirasawa. The cherry trees along the embankment are in full bloom, so heavy with flowers the branches sag over the path, and every time the wind comes down off the mountains the whole tunnel lets go at once.  #c1_0053
> Up on the hill above it all, where the shrine is, the Ōzakura is blooming too: one cherry tree older than anyone's records, so big that from the bridge it looks like a pink cloud caught on the hillside.  #c1_0260
